This has been probably done before but just in case, not yet, below is the work around that I did. (while waiting for the solution),
1. In the call to **softRemove**, I added a data in the **SaveOptions** parameter.
`this.repo.softRemove(entity, {data: { deleted: true } });`
2. Then in the subscriber, I checked the data in the **beforeUpdate** method. (depending on the need, can also be done in **afterUpdate**). I used this data to determine whether the operation was a delete/remove.
`if (event.queryRunner.data.deleted) {
    // extra delete logic
}`

